  "feature_instruction": "This feature implements the complete frontend authentication flow for MultiFit Aundh, enabling users to log in, register, and protecting routes based on their authentication status. It consists of a React Context (`AuthContext.tsx`) to manage global authentication state, a custom hook (`useAuth.ts`) for easy access to this context, a service (`authService.ts`) for interacting with the backend authentication API, TypeScript types (`auth.ts`) for data structures, a login page (`LoginPage.tsx`), and a route protection component (`ProtectedRoute.tsx`).\n\n## Design Tokens\n- Navbar: bg-[#1A1A1A] text-[#F5F5F5]\n- Primary CTA: bg-[#DFFF00] hover:bg-[#DFFF00]/90 text-[#1A1A1A] font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200\n- Brand text accent: text-[#DFFF00]\n- Section bg: bg-[#F5F5F5] (odd sections) / bg-gray-50 (even sections)\n- Card: bg-white rounded-xl shadow-md border border-gray-100 p-6\n- Section container: <section className=\"py-16 px-4\"><div className=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto\">\n- Hero h1: text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white\n- Body: text-gray-700 leading-relaxed\n- Form input: border border-gray-300 rounded-md px-4 py-2 focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#DFFF00] focus:border-transparent\n- Error text: text-red-500 text-sm mt-1\n\n## AuthContext.tsx\nThis file defines the `AuthContext` and `AuthContextProvider` component. It manages the global authentication state, including the currently logged-in `user` (of type `User | null`), the `token` (string | null), `isAuthenticated` (boolean), and `loading` (boolean).\n\n1.  **State Management**: Use `useState` for `user`, `token`, `isAuthenticated`, and `loading`. `loading` should be true initially and when performing auth operations.\n2.  **Initial Load**: On component mount, check `localStorage` for the key `'token'`. If found, attempt to decode it to populate the `user` state and set `isAuthenticated` to true. If the token is invalid or expired, clear it from `localStorage` and reset the state.\n3.  **`login(credentials: AuthRequest): Promise<void>`**: \n    *   Sets `loading` to `true`.\n    *   Calls `authService.login(credentials)`.\n    *   On success, extracts `jwtToken` from the `AuthResponse`.\n    *   Stores `jwtToken` in `localStorage` using the key `'token'`.\n    *   Decodes the `jwtToken` to extract user details (id, email, firstName, lastName, roles). Assume the decoded token payload has `userId`, `sub` (for email), `firstName`, `lastName`, and `roles` (an array of strings like `['ROLE_USER', 'ROLE_ADMIN']`).\n    *   Sets `user` state with the decoded user details, `token` state with `jwtToken`, and `isAuthenticated` to `true`.\n    *   Sets `loading` to `false`.\n    *   On error, sets `loading` to `false` and throws the error.\n4.  **`register(userData: AuthRequest): Promise<void>`**: \n    *   Sets `loading` to `true`.\n    *   Calls `authService.register(userData)`.\n    *   On success, extracts `jwtToken` from the `AuthResponse`.\n    *   Stores `jwtToken` in `localStorage` using the key `'token'`.\n    *   Decodes the `jwtToken` to extract user details (id, email, firstName, lastName, roles).\n    *   Sets `user` state with the decoded user details, `token` state with `jwtToken`, and `isAuthenticated` to `true`.\n    *   Sets `loading` to `false`.\n    *   On error, sets `loading` to `false` and throws the error.\n5.  **`logout(): void`**: \n    *   Removes the `'token'` key from `localStorage`.\n    *   Resets `user` to `null`, `token` to `null`, and `isAuthenticated` to `false`.\n6.  **Context Value**: The `AuthContext.Provider` should provide an object containing `user`, `token`, `isAuthenticated`, `loading`, `login`, `register`, and `logout`.\n\n## useAuth.ts\nThis custom React hook provides a convenient way for components to access the authentication context.\n1.  **`useAuth()`**: Calls `useContext(AuthContext)` and returns the context value directly.\n\n## authService.ts\nThis service handles communication with the backend authentication API.\n1.  **`login(credentials: AuthRequest): Promise<AuthResponse>`**: \n    *   Makes a POST request to `/api/v1/auth/login` with `credentials` as the request body.\n    *   Uses the `axios` instance from `frontend/src/api/client.ts`.\n    *   Returns the `AuthResponse` from the backend.\n2.  **`register(userData: AuthRequest): Promise<AuthResponse>`**: \n    *   Makes a POST request to `/api/v1/auth/register` with `userData` as the request body.\n    *   Uses the `axios` instance from `frontend/src/api/client.ts`.\n    *   Returns the `AuthResponse` from the backend.\n\n## auth.ts\nThis file defines the TypeScript interfaces for authentication-related data structures.\n1.  **`AuthRequest`**: Interface for login/registration request payload, matching `shared-backend`'s `AuthRequest` (`email: string`, `password: string`).\n2.  **`AuthResponse`**: Interface for login/registration response payload, matching `shared-backend`'s `AuthResponse` (`jwtToken: string`).\n3.  **`User`**: Interface representing the authenticated user's details, derived from the JWT payload (`id: string`, `email: string`, `firstName: string`, `lastName: string`, `roles: string[]`).\n4.  **`AuthContextType`**: Interface for the shape of the authentication context value.\n\n## LoginPage.tsx\nThis page provides the user interface for logging in.\n1.  **Layout**: Wrap the page content in the `<Layout>` component from `shared-ui`.\n2.  **Form**: Create a form with input fields for `email` and `password`. Use `useState` to manage form input values.\n3.  **Authentication**: Use the `useAuth` hook to access the `login` function and `isAuthenticated` state.\n4.  **Submission**: On form submission, call `login({ email, password })`.\n5.  **Redirection**: If `isAuthenticated` becomes `true` (after successful login), redirect the user to the home page (`/`) using `react-router-dom`'s `useNavigate` hook.\n6.  **Error Handling**: Display error messages if login fails (e.g., "Invalid credentials").\n7.  **Design**: Apply design tokens for a bold and energetic look.\n    *   Hero section with a background image: `url(https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534438327276-14e5300c3a48?w=1920&q=80)` with an `absolute inset-0 bg-black bg-opacity-50` overlay.\n    *   Headline: `h1` with text \"Ignite Your Potential\" and sub-headline \"Welcome Back, Champion!\" using `text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white`.\n    *   Form container: `bg-white p-8 rounded-lg shadow-lg max-w-md mx-auto`.\n    *   Input fields: `border border-gray-300 rounded-md px-4 py-2 w-full focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#DFFF00] focus:border-transparent`.\n    *   Login button: `bg-[#DFFF00] hover:bg-[#DFFF00]/90 text-[#1A1A1A] font-semibold rounded-full px-8 py-3 transition-all duration-200 w-full` with text \"Login\".\n    *   Link to registration (if applicable): \"Don't have an account? <Link to='/register' className='text-[#DFFF00] hover:underline'>Sign Up</Link>\"\n\n## ProtectedRoute.tsx\nThis component acts as a wrapper to restrict access to its children routes to authenticated users.\n1.  **Authentication Check**: Use the `useAuth` hook to get `isAuthenticated` and `loading` states.\n2.  **Loading State**: If `loading` is `true`, render a simple loading indicator (e.g., a `div` with text \"Loading...\").\n3.  **Redirection**: If `loading` is `false` and `isAuthenticated` is `false`, redirect the user to the `/login` page using `react-router-dom`'s `Navigate` component.\n4.  **Render Children**: If `isAuthenticated` is `true`, render the `children` prop.\n",
